== 2.3 Neo-Determinism: Stop-and-Go Determinism (Sustainable Middle Path)
Unchecked Possibilism unleashed severe crises: stratospheric ozone depletion, global warming, receding glaciers, desertification, and biodiversity loss. In response, Australian geographer *Griffith Taylor* formulated *Neo-Determinism* or *Stop-and-Go Determinism*.

#important-box(title: "The Essence of Neo-Determinism")[
  Neo-Determinism is a *Middle Path* (*Madhyam Marg*) rejecting both absolute necessity and absolute freedom:
  - Humans can alter the rate, but not the ultimate direction, of progress.
  - Humankind conquers nature only by obeying its non-negotiable ecological laws.
]

*The Traffic Light Analogy:*
- *Red Light (Stop):* Pause development when environmental thresholds are breached (e.g., desertification, over-drafted aquifers).
- *Amber Light (Prepare):* Monitor carrying capacity, conduct environmental assessments, and develop green alternatives.
- *Green Light (Go):* Advance development within sustainable ecological carrying limits.

